<h3>Read one row as a joint probability</h3>
<p>The row for <code>cat</code> says that the first letter is c <strong>and</strong> the second letter is a <strong>and</strong> the third letter is t. Its joint probability is 0.18. In event notation, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline" aria-label="P of L one equals c, L two equals a, and L three equals t, equals zero point one eight"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0.18</mn></mrow></math>.</p>
<h3>Find a marginal probability by adding rows</h3>
<p>A <strong>marginal probability</strong> keeps the letter position we care about and ignores the others. &ldquo;Ignore&rdquo; does not mean discard their probability. It means add the probabilities of every row that has the value we want.</p>
